<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Ferrara</h1><p class="st-meta">1101 CE – 1264 CE (approx.) · capital Ferrara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Po delta city-republic whose factional wars ended with the Este family as perpetual lords, the start of one of Italy's great dynasties.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-tuscany">Matilda of Canossa</a>, who besieged it in 1101 to put down a revolt. In the years that followed, citizens formed a commune under consuls, profiting from Po river traffic and salt. The cathedral was begun in 1135.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consuls</a> and later a podestà ruled, but power was really contested between noble factions: the Adelardi, the Ghibelline Torelli led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salinguerra-ii-torelli">Salinguerra II Torelli</a>, and the Guelph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-este">Este</a> marquises. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara's</a> position on the Po made it a hub for trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> plain. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzo-vii-deste">Azzo VII d'Este</a> expelled Salinguerra in 1240 with Venetian and papal help.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzo-vii-deste">Azzo VII</a>'s death in 1264, the citizens proclaimed his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obizzo-ii-deste">Obizzo II d'Este</a> perpetual lord, and the commune gave way to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-ferrara">Duchy of Ferrara</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-este">Este</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1101 CE – 1264 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.61%;width:3.24%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1101 CE – 1264 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ferrara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Salinguerra II Torelli, Azzo VII d'Este</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ferrara (commune)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1182&amp;focus=commune-of-ferrara" aria-label="Commune of Ferrara on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4957 593 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Ferrara lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5277 849L5277 849"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5277 849h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5277 849h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5277 849h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ferrara. <a href="/atlas?year=1182&amp;focus=commune-of-ferrara">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
